Z||000002||Shaun41178||12-28-2000||02:42 AM||||I would say that without a doubt Steve Hamm is making the most hp and tq from a 2.8 liter.  I beleive he has dynoed around 300 hp at the wheels.  I dont' know specifics but I do know that it is a prepped engine running a turbo at around 10 psi of boost.  He burns rubber through three gears and has toasted many a trannies.  he had a small website up but I don't know where that is at.<P>A 2.8 with a slightly higher compression, bigger cam, ported heads, good valve job, ported TB, ported exhaust, cat-back can make about 170 or so at the flywheel with the stock computer.  Get  Haltech and one can use a much bigger cam and get around 200 or so.  I do know that back in the 80's race teams were getting 270 hp from 2.8's but they had carbs and were not computer controlled and had radical cams.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Will||12-28-2000||09:53 AM||||If your going to do the swap anyway, go with a 3.4. You can do all the same mods to the 3.4 as you can to the 2.8, but as they say, there's no replacement for displacement.<BR>||||reg||1
